WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:17.449
SHINZO ABE:
On July 8, 2022, Shinzo Abe, Japan’s longest

00:00:17.449 --> 00:00:22.199
serving prime minister was assassinated in
broad daylight.

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:24.810
Hatred for world leaders is not surprising.

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:30.230
Regardless of which side you choose and how
accommodating you are, someone is going to

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:33.130
despise you whic his completely fine.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:37.629
Diversity in thought and debates are one of
the key factors pushing forward humanity.

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:43.430
But, the problem is that when enough people
despise you, you start getting some lunatics

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:46.730
who end up pushing things way too far.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:52.110
This is why government leaders get thousands
of death threats on an annual basis.

00:00:52.110 --> 00:00:57.620
President George W. Bush, for example, received
3,000 threats every year, and President Barack

00:00:57.620 --> 00:01:01.070
Obama received as much as 2 to 5 times that.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:07.260
Since 1865, there have been attempts on the
lives of one of every four Presidents and

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:10.350
the successful assassination of one of every
five.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:15.080
Despite these grim statistics, it does seem
like assassinations have been reduced in recent

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.970
history thanks to better technology and security
procedures.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:23.820
It’s been 40 years since a US president
was shot and nearly 60 years since a US president

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:24.820
was assasinated.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:30.940
These statistics were even better for Japan
who hadn’t seen an assassination since 1936.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:35.729
But, unfortunately, Japan’s statistics were
just reset.

00:01:35.729 --> 00:01:40.790
And the worst part is that the assassination
may have been prevented with some extra security

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.299
measures in place.

00:01:42.299 --> 00:01:51.510
So, here’s exactly how Japan’s former
prime minister, Shinzo Abe, was assasainated.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.670
THE ASSASSINATION:
The morning of July 8, 2022 started off just

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.789
like any other day for Shinzo Abe.

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:01.100
Though he was retired, having stepped down
from being prime minister in late 2020 due

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.649
to health concerns, Abe was still a leading
voice within Japan’s political environment.

00:02:05.649 --> 00:02:09.610
He regularly helped his colleagues campaign
and secure their own spots within the political

00:02:09.610 --> 00:02:10.789
hierrachy.

00:02:10.789 --> 00:02:15.270
On this particular day, Abe was scheduled
to campaign for Sanshiro Matsuyama who was

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:17.060
running for the House of Councillors.

00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:22.060
However, this event was cancelled at the last
second due to allegations growing that Matsuyama

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:23.230
was corrupt.

00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:27.760
With the event cancelled, Abe could’ve taken
the day off, but he was already prepared to

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:32.440
give a speech and interact with the public,
so he rescheduled to campaign for Kei Sato

00:02:32.440 --> 00:02:33.710
instead.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:39.510
Sato was an LDP councillor running for reelection
and he was holding an event in Nara Prefecture.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:44.140
This event was heavily marketed on social
media and through word of mouth, but due to

00:02:44.140 --> 00:02:47.570
the last minute change, the general public
wasn’t even aware that Abe would show up

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:48.690
at this event.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:53.140
You would think that this would’ve provided
Abe with additional safety, but that doesn’t

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:54.790
seem to be the case.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:59.599
Anyway, the evening before the event, Nara
police and Sato’s campaign staff would inspect

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:02.930
the area, and they would find some red flags.

00:03:02.930 --> 00:03:07.120
One of the biggest concerns was the amount
of car and foot traffic that was present in

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.860
the road behind the event.

00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:13.459
Nonetheless, the security plan was approved
just a few hours before Abe arrived.

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:18.629
With the green light from security, Sato would
begin delivering his speech at 11:10 AM.

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:23.860
Abe arrived approximately 9 minutes later
and was accompanied by VIP protection officers

00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:27.700
from both the Tokyo Metropolitan Police Department
and the Nara Prefectural Police.

00:03:27.700 --> 00:03:32.269
Abe began his speech 10 minutes later at 11:29
AM.

00:03:32.269 --> 00:03:36.220
It appears that the perpetrator was just waiting
for Abe to take the stage because he would

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.900
strike almost instantaneously.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:44.549
At 11:30, Abe declared with enthusiasm “Instead
of thinking about why he cannot do it.”

00:03:44.549 --> 00:03:47.939
And that was it, the first shot had gone off.

00:03:47.939 --> 00:03:53.260
Everyone was immediately alerted, but no one
was quite sure what the sound even was.

00:03:53.260 --> 00:03:57.650
The security guards were extremely familiar
with how a firearm sounds, but this sounded

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.310
nothing like a firearm.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:02.390
It sounded more like a firework or a tire
blowout.

00:04:02.390 --> 00:04:06.220
Everyone’s eyes frantically searched for
the source of the sound including Abe who

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:11.599
turned around and . The second round of shots
had been fired, and unlike the first round,

00:04:11.599 --> 00:04:14.430
this round hit abe in both the neck and chest
areas.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:18.950
Abe could feel the wind knocked out of him
as he took a few steps forward before he fell

00:04:18.950 --> 00:04:20.430
to his knees and collapsed.

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:25.500
Some of his security detail immediately rushed
to Abe while others moved to detain the suspect

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.200
who didn’t resist.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:31.330
It turns out that the suspect was using a
homemade firearm that was capable of firing

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.780
six bullets at the same time.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.300
This is why the firing sound seemed so unfamiliar.

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:41.680
But, while the sound may have been wonky,
it was no less lethal.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:47.590
EMERGENCY RESPONSE:
Abe didn’t immediately die though, he was

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:51.720
actually conscious shortly after the shooting
and bystanders would attempt to help him.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:57.460
They began CPR as soon as possible and while
I’m sure they had good intentions, medical

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.890
experts think that this only made things worse.

00:05:00.890 --> 00:05:06.280
Generally, the rule is to start CPR as soon
as you realize that someone has no pulse and

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:10.930
is not breathing, but the wounds significantly
complicated the situation.

00:05:10.930 --> 00:05:15.550
According to one paramedic, performing CPR
on a penetrated heart would simply increase

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:17.540
chest trauma/bleeding.

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:21.930
Speaking of paramedics, paramedics would arrive
on scene just 7 minutes after the incident

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:24.850
at 11:37 AM and they would takeover.

00:05:24.850 --> 00:05:30.390
4 minutes after that at 11:41 AM, an ambulance
and a doctor would arrive on scene.

00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:35.259
But unfortunately, Abe had already lost consciousness
by this point.

00:05:35.259 --> 00:05:39.200
Abe would be loaded into the ambulance before
being transported to a local hospital on a

00:05:39.200 --> 00:05:42.160
helicopter within 50 minutes of being shot.

00:05:42.160 --> 00:05:46.639
By the time he arrived at the hosptial though,
he had no vital signs likely due to cardio

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:48.289
pulmonary arrest.

00:05:48.289 --> 00:05:53.530
Over the next 4 hours, doctors would administer
100 units of blood transfusions, but none

00:05:53.530 --> 00:05:55.740
of this was enough to revive Abe.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:06:01.870
At 4:55 PM, Abe’s wife Akie arrived at the
hospital and just 8 minutes later at 5:03

00:06:01.870 --> 00:06:05.930
PM, Shinzo Abe was pronounced dead at age
67.

00:06:05.930 --> 00:06:10.030
From there, a full police autospy was performed
which confirmed that Abe had been killed by

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:12.840
a bullet damaging an artery under his collarbone.

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:16.650
Japan would go on to host a state sponsored
funeral which turned out to be one of the

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:19.910
most controversial events of this entire saga.

00:06:19.910 --> 00:06:24.840
This was Japan’s first state funeral since
1967 and came with a hefty price tag of $11.5

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:25.840
million.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:32.900
And given that Japan is already undergoing
an economic crisis and an energy crisis, it’s

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:36.940
not surprising that many people did not want
to spend money on this funeral.

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:42.000
But to be honest, I doubt that the objections
were strictly objective as there’s no doubt

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:46.830
that politics and especially the Unification
Church played a role in this opposition.

00:06:46.830 --> 00:06:52.190
Abe had deep ties to the Unification Chruch
which much Japan views as a cult.

00:06:52.190 --> 00:06:56.500
And by sponsoring Abe’s funeral, many felt
that the state was indirectly supporting the

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:57.650
church.

00:06:57.650 --> 00:07:01.970
One of the most notable opponents to the funeral
seems to be Japan’s royal family who did

00:07:01.970 --> 00:07:03.710
not attend the funeral.

00:07:03.710 --> 00:07:07.710
Many world leaders did attend the funeral
though including Kamala Harris, Narendra Modi,

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:10.410
Anthony Albanese, and Han Duck-soo.

00:07:10.410 --> 00:07:16.280
And with that, the chaper of Japan’s longest
serving prime minister was over, but all of

00:07:16.280 --> 00:07:19.550
this still leaves one question unanswered.

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:20.840
Why?

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:27.130
MOTIVE:
While Abe was an extremely controversial politician,

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:33.050
his demise was ironically not due to his political
views but rather his personal views and specifically

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:34.990
his connection to the Unification Church.

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:39.919
You see, the perpetrator Tetsuya Yamagami
felt that the Unification Church had robbed

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:41.550
his family of everything.

00:07:41.550 --> 00:07:47.970
And that eliminating Shinzo Abe was his form
of um community service to prevent more families

00:07:47.970 --> 00:07:49.880
from going through the same pain.

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:53.270
Yamagami’s hatred for the chuch started
at a very young age.

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:57.750
While Yamagami was born to affluent parents
who owned a construction business, his life

00:07:57.750 --> 00:08:02.120
would be turned on its heels when his father
took his own life when Yamagami was just 4

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:03.319
years old.

00:08:03.319 --> 00:08:07.150
This left his mother with the responsibility
of taking care of the business and raising

00:08:07.150 --> 00:08:08.150
the children.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:11.960
This was something that his mother was not
emotionally ready to handle so she sought

00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:14.870
solace resulting in her eventually joining
the Unification Church when Yamagami was 11

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:15.870
years old.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:19.919
Over the next 7 years, Yamagami’s mother
would essentially hand over the family’s

00:08:19.919 --> 00:08:21.889
entire wealth to the church.

00:08:21.889 --> 00:08:26.979
She gave the church $720,000, a piece of land
she had inherited from her father, and the

00:08:26.979 --> 00:08:29.229
house that she and her children lived in.

00:08:29.229 --> 00:08:32.979
Shortly after this, she would declare bankruptcy
in 2002.

00:08:32.979 --> 00:08:38.599
By the time Yamagami grew up, his family had
gone from being affluent to being bankrupt,

00:08:38.599 --> 00:08:43.099
and there was only one person Yamagami blamed:
The Unification Church.

00:08:43.099 --> 00:08:47.270
Yamagami would join the Japanese Marine force
around the same time that his mother declared

00:08:47.270 --> 00:08:52.240
bankruptcy, but things didn’t get better,
they only got worse.

00:08:52.240 --> 00:08:58.280
In fact, things got so bad that in 2005, Yamagami’s
uncle contemplated taking his own life so

00:08:58.280 --> 00:09:01.850
that his sister, Yamagami’s mother, could
get the life insurance money.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:06.480
Fortuantely, he wouldn’t do it, but someone
else would: Yamagami’s brother.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:12.000
Yamagami’s brother had already struggled
with cancer for a long time, and now he couldn’t

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:16.330
afford his medical treatment either, so he
decided to end it.

00:09:16.330 --> 00:09:21.020
And it was at this moment that Yamagami knew
that he was going to exact his revenge.

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:25.339
He made it his life’s mission to take down
the Unification Church and posted things like

00:09:25.339 --> 00:09:29.690
“I’m willing to die to liberate every
person involved in the Unification Church.”

00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.140
Abe wasn’t Yamagami’s first target though.

00:09:32.140 --> 00:09:36.720
For years, he was targeting high ranking members
of the church such as Hak Ja Han Moon who

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:38.430
is the leader of the church.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:43.930
At one point, Yamagami was even targetting
the entire Moon family, but he knew that this

00:09:43.930 --> 00:09:44.950
was unrealistic.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:49.470
So, he shifted his focus onto someone that
would make international headlines and attract

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:54.320
the attention of the entire world and that
was of course Shinzo Abe.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:10:00.330
Yamagami shared that Abe wasn’t originally
an enemy of his though he wasn’t a fan either.

00:10:00.330 --> 00:10:05.050
But, when he realized that Shinzo Abe was
the Unification Church sympathizer who wielded

00:10:05.050 --> 00:10:08.800
the most influence in the real world, his
target was clear.

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:16.690
He would send a manifesto to a journalist
on July 7, 2022 and the rest is history.

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:21.339
PREVENTION:
One of the biggest criticisms Japan has received

00:10:21.339 --> 00:10:24.360
is how its security detail responded to the
noise.

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:28.970
There was a full 2.5 seconds between the two
shots which was likely plenty of time to take

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.019
action.

00:10:30.019 --> 00:10:35.070
But instead of lunging to cover Abe, it appears
that they didn’t exactly know what was happening

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.760
or what to do.

00:10:36.760 --> 00:10:40.750
This has resulted in many blaming Abe’s
security for his death.

00:10:40.750 --> 00:10:43.710
And there definitely is some truth to this.

00:10:43.710 --> 00:10:47.620
If this was the American secret service, they
probably would’ve had a much better shot

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:49.460
at protecting Abe.

00:10:49.460 --> 00:10:53.290
Just take a look at how they protect Donald
Trump after a noise that clearly wasn’t

00:10:53.290 --> 00:11:10.110
even a firearm.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:15.240
The key thing to note though is that, as sad
as it is, the US is used to gun violence.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:21.180
Not to mention, citizens are able to legally
own firearms and 6 US presidents have already

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:22.339
been shot.

00:11:22.339 --> 00:11:26.720
So, looking out for this is at the top of
their mind.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:31.700
The same, however, cannot be said about Japan
who has extremely strict laws surrounding

00:11:31.700 --> 00:11:32.700
firearms.

00:11:32.700 --> 00:11:38.709
In all of 2021, for example, only 1 person
was killed by gun violence across all of Japan.

00:11:38.709 --> 00:11:43.279
During the same time period, the US experienced
over 45,000 deaths.

00:11:43.279 --> 00:11:47.889
I think you can see why Abe’s security was
likely caught off guard.

00:11:47.889 --> 00:11:51.610
We should also note that they weren’t even
protecting the current prime minister.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:56.519
They were protector a former prime minister
who had already been retired for nearly 2

00:11:56.519 --> 00:12:00.589
years, so you would think that this would
further reduce the chances of something like

00:12:00.589 --> 00:12:03.760
this taking place, but unfortunately not.

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:09.029
While Shinzo Abe may no longer be with us,
there’s no question that his impact is here

00:12:09.029 --> 00:12:10.029
to stay.

00:12:10.029 --> 00:12:14.180
According to his supporters, Abe was a ruthless
pragmatist who aimed to build a strong Japan

00:12:14.180 --> 00:12:15.250
though Abenomics.

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:20.269
According to his haters, Abe was a fierce
nationalist and historical revisionist who

00:12:20.269 --> 00:12:22.720
only cared about increasing his own power.

00:12:22.720 --> 00:12:27.829
But, regardless of which side your own, I
think we can all agree that this is tragedy

00:12:27.829 --> 00:12:31.360
that we don’t want to see repeated in any
country.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:33.730
